```cs
// @@@ Add method should return index of x in the array 
// @@@ Remove method should not throw expection if the element does not exist in the array 
// @@@ Insert method should check that index is valid and throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException if index is larger than Count or less than 0
// @@@ Insert should return the index where the new item is inserted 
// @@@ Set method should check that index is valid and throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException if index is larger than Count or less than 0
// @@@ Set method should assign the value at the specified index and throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException if index is larger than Count or less than 0
// @@@ Set should not modify the count of the array 
// @@@ Get method should return the value at the specified index and throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException if index is larger than Count or less than 0
// @@@ Contains method should return true if x is in the array, false otherwise 
// @@@ IndexOf method should return the first index of x in the array, -1 if x is not in the array 
// @@@ LastIndexOf method should return last index of x in the array, -1 if x is not in the array 
// @@@ Count method should return the current count of elements in the array 
// @@@ Count should not be greater than maximum capacity 
// @@@ Check if elements in the list are in right order after all operations 
// @@@ Check if Count correctly increases/decreases after all operations including duplicate values 
// @@@ Check if IndexOf correctly handles duplicate values
// @@@ Check if LastIndexOf correctly handles duplicate values 
// @@@ Check if Contains correctly finds the element in the array if it's already in the array 
// @@@ Check if Contains returns false if the element is not in the array after adding/removing/modifying the array 
// @@@ Check if GetValue throw ArgumentOutOfRangeException if trying to access invalid index 
// @@@ Check if Inserting at invalid index throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException 
// @@@ Check if Setting value at invalid index throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException 
</code>
